nment actions, validating the reasonableness of the grounds for denial in information-access decisions and issuing rulings across five types of decisions: Provimento (grant), Provimento parcial (partial grant), Desprovimento (denial), Não conhecimento (not processed), and Perda de objeto (moot). Overall, CGU functions as the central internal control authority, coordinating information governance, auditing practices, compliance with the LAI, and the authoritative processing and review of information-access decisions across the federal government."}, "metrics": {"attempted_request_count": 1, "successful_response_count": 0, "failed_response_count": 0, "responses_with_tokens": 1, "prompt_tokens": 520, "completion_tokens": 1941, "total_tokens": 2461, "compute_duration_seconds": 16.20081615447998, "streaming_responses": 0, "retries": 0, "requests_with_retries": 0}}}